#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:1
msgid "Model Insertion from Fuel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:3
msgid ""
"Gazebo Fuel hosts hundreds of models that can easily be added to a world "
"running in the Gazebo GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:6
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:8
msgid "Start by getting Gazebo up and running with an empty world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:10
msgid "gz sim empty.sdf\n"
msgstr "gz sim empty.sdf\n"

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:14
msgid ""
"The previous tutorial, [Manipulating Models](manipulating_models.md), shows "
"you how to interact with models, which might be helpful once you add some "
"Fuel models to your world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:16
msgid "Choose a Model"
msgstr "選擇模型"

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:18
msgid ""
"Fuel's model collection is at [app.gazebosim.org/fuel/models](https://app."
"gazebosim.org/fuel/models). Head over and browse the available content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:21
msgid "![Fuel models preview](tutorials/fuel_insert/fuel.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:21
msgid "Fuel models preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:23
msgid ""
"Click on any one of the thumbnails, or use the search bar. For example, "
"let's find the [Mine Cart Engine](https://app.gazebosim.org/OpenRobotics/"
"fuel/models/Mine%20Cart%20Engine)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:26
msgid "![Vent](tutorials/fuel_insert/mine_cart_engine_detail.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:26
msgid "Vent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:28
msgid ""
"Note that some of the model files are quite large and may take some time to "
"download into your world. Check that the file size on the right is "
"reasonable for your application before moving on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:31
msgid "Spawn a Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:33
msgid "There are a few different ways to spawn a model into the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:35
msgid "**Spawn from 'Fuel resources' using the Resource Spawner plugin.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:37
msgid ""
"Select the Resource Spawner plugin from the plugin menu (top right corner).  "
"The plugin will appear in the right panel, you might need to scroll down to "
"be able to see the plugin.   Wait until the resources are loaded under the "
"'Fuel resources' panel.   Select a resource owner (e.g. openrobotics), you "
"can now search for the model name in the right panel.   Click on the cloud "
"icon to download the model.   When the model has been downloaded, you can "
"click on the model and insert it into your simulation scene."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:44
msgid ""
"![Resource Spawner - Fuel resources](tutorials/fuel_insert/"
"resource_spawner_cloud.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:44 ../../../fuel_insert.md:55
msgid "Resource Spawner - Fuel resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:47
msgid ""
"**Download model files from Fuel and spawn from local sources using the "
"Resource Spawner plugin.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:49
msgid ""
"Download the model files from [app.gazebosim.org/fuel/models](https://app."
"gazebosim.org/fuel/models)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:50
msgid ""
"Extract the files and place them under your local model directory (e.g. `~/"
"my-local-models/model-name`).  The folder should contain `materials`, "
"`meshes` as well as the `model.config` and the `model.sdf` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:52
msgid ""
"Add your model directory as a resource with `export GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=~/"
"my-local-models/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:53
msgid ""
"Open the Gazebo Simulator and add the Resource Spawner Plugin, the model "
"should now show up under your local resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:55
msgid ""
"![Resource Spawner - Fuel resources](tutorials/fuel_insert/"
"resource_spawner_local.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:57
msgid ""
"**Copying the SDF snippet and adding it to your custom world SDF file.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:59
msgid ""
"With the `<>` button you can directly copy an SDF snippet to paste into your "
"world SDF file.   The SDF snippet will look something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:62
msgid ""
"<include>\n"
"  <uri>\n"
"    https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Mine Cart Engine\n"
"  </uri>\n"
"</include>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:70
msgid ""
"You can then add that snippet to a world SDF file as shown in the animation "
"below.   More information on how to build your own world SDF files can be "
"found in the tutorial on [SDF Worlds](sdf_worlds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:73
msgid "![spawn](tutorials/fuel_insert/husky.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:73
msgid "spawn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:75
msgid ""
"**Downloading the code to permanently add a Fuel model to your custom SDF "
"file.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:77
msgid ""
"If you prefer to add a Fuel model permanently to an `sdf` file, you can just "
"as easily download the code by clicking the download-arrow icon to the right "
"of the model's image.  Look at the tutorial on [SDF Worlds](sdf_worlds) for "
"more information on how to construct a custom world SDF file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:80
msgid ""
"Now you can add more models, or even load in any one of the plugins you "
"learned about to interact with the model the same way you could with the "
"shapes in the previous tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:82
msgid "Next Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../fuel_insert.md:84
msgid ""
"Now that you know how to add models hosted on Gazebo Fuel, it is time to "
"learn how to [Build Your Own Robot](building_robot)."
msgstr ""
